## 🔍 Why File Uploads Matter in Express

File uploads allow users to send files (images, PDFs, etc.) to your server using forms or APIs.

Examples:

* Profile picture uploads
* Resume submissions
* CSV bulk importers
* Image uploads for blogs or products

But handling them *safely*, *efficiently*, and *scalably* is the real dev challenge.

---

## 🧰 Middleware: `multer` — the de facto solution

Express doesn’t parse multipart/form-data (file uploads) by default. For that, we use:

```bash
npm install multer
```

> Multer handles `multipart/form-data` and stores uploaded files in memory or disk with full control 
over size, type, naming, etc.

---

## 🛠 Basic Setup

```js
const express = require('express');
const multer = require('multer');
const app = express();

// Configure storage
const storage = multer.diskStorage({
  destination: function (req, file, cb) {
    cb(null, './uploads'); // folder where files will be saved
  },
  filename: function (req, file, cb) {
    const uniqueSuffix = Date.now() + '-' + Math.round(Math.random() * 1E9);
    cb(null, uniqueSuffix + '-' + file.originalname);
  }
});

// Create middleware
const upload = multer({ storage });

// Upload single file
app.post('/upload', upload.single('avatar'), (req, res) => {
  console.log(req.file); // Metadata about uploaded file
  res.send('File uploaded!');
});
```

---

## 🔬 Anatomy of `req.file`

```json
{
  "fieldname": "avatar",
  "originalname": "photo.png",
  "encoding": "7bit",
  "mimetype": "image/png",
  "destination": "./uploads",
  "filename": "162836381-photo.png",
  "path": "uploads/162836381-photo.png",
  "size": 12345
}
```

---

## ⚙️ Options & Control

### ✅ Upload multiple files:

```js
upload.array('photos', 5)
```

### ✅ Upload specific fields:

```js
upload.fields([
  { name: 'avatar', maxCount: 1 },
  { name: 'resume', maxCount: 1 }
]);
```

### ✅ Memory Storage (buffer instead of saving to disk):

```js
const storage = multer.memoryStorage();
```

### ✅ File filters (only allow images):

```js
const upload = multer({
  storage,
  fileFilter: function (req, file, cb) {
    if (file.mimetype.startsWith("image/")) {
      cb(null, true);
    } else {
      cb(new Error("Only images allowed!"), false);
    }
  }
});
```

---

## 🔐 Security Best Practices

| Concern              | Solution                                 |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| File name conflicts  | Use timestamp or UUID                    |
| Large file sizes     | Set limits (`limits: { fileSize: 1MB }`) |
| Directory traversal  | Validate filenames                       |
| Executable uploads   | Restrict `mimetype`, scan files          |
| DoS via many uploads | Rate-limit, or throttle upload API       |

