## 🚫 Common Mistakes in Express MVC

| Mistake                           | Why it's bad                               |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Mixing model logic in controllers | Tight coupling, can't reuse logic          |
| Controllers doing too much        | Becomes unreadable and hard to test        |
| Skipping router layer             | Hard to manage paths and middleware        |
| No `middlewares/` folder          | Middleware logic clogs up app.js           |
| Views + API in same controller    | Separation of API vs. rendered HTML breaks |

---

## 🔐 Middleware in MVC

MVC doesn't **require** middleware, but real-world projects always use it.

Example:

* `authMiddleware.js` – checks if user is authenticated before continuing
* `errorHandler.js` – wraps all controllers in a try-catch layer

You can apply middleware:

```js
router.post('/dashboard', authMiddleware, dashboardController.show);
```

